# Pages this app must have exported, checked by scripts/check-export.sh.
# One path per line, relative to the export root (apps/docs/out).
#
# These are the sections that go missing WITHOUT breaking anything else, so a
# page count and a nav check both stay green while the section is gone:
#
#   docs/services/   generated at build time by scripts/gen-services-nav.ts from
#                    @hanzo/products. When that package does not resolve the
#                    script warns and keeps the committed meta.json, so a broken
#                    catalog is a warning in a log nobody reads.
#   docs/studio/     a git submodule (hanzo-docs/studio-docs). A checkout that
#                    does not recurse leaves the directory empty and the section
#                    simply does not exist in the output.
#   docs/mcp-tools/  one page per MCP tool, generated by scripts/gen-mcp-pages.ts
#                    from the vendored tools/list answer. It is the largest
#                    section in the site and the easiest to lose whole: drop the
#                    generator from pre-build and every other page still builds.
docs/services/index.html
docs/studio/index.html
docs/mcp-tools/index.html
docs/mcp-tools/all-tools/index.html
#
#   llms-full.txt    the whole corpus in one fetch, and llms.mdx/ the per-page
#   llms.mdx/        markdown twin every page's Copy Markdown / View Markdown /
#                    Open in ChatGPT button points at. Both come from route
#                    handlers, so losing them is silent in the worst way: the
#                    HTML still builds, the buttons still render, and they go
#                    back to fetching 404s — which is the state this gate was
#                    added to end.
llms.txt
llms-full.txt
llms.mdx/docs/content.md
